<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    The Jawa world's biome mix. Owner-ratified; gate W3.
    Tiers from VISION (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/tidally_locked_world.md, 6370746);
    the offset NUMBERS are CREATE's, and the reasoning for them is below because
    the units are not what anyone would guess.

    🔴 WORLDGEN-GATED. Biome scoring runs once, in WorldGenStep_Terrain at order 0.
    A patch that misses a worldgen never touches that world.
    ⭐ THIS FILE IS KEPT because it configures the game that produces the SOURCE
    world Ash'karr is painted from — an input to the external map, not an in-game
    worldgen feature of ours. The final map arrives through the live bridge.

    WHY THIS PATCHES THE SHIPPED TidallyLocked DEF RATHER THAN ADDING OUR OWN.
    AlienWorlds keeps exactly ONE active PlanetTypeDef (PlanetTypeManager
    .activePlanetType, chosen in mod settings, scribed per save). A second def
    would REPLACE tidal lock and silently drop the temperature curve this whole
    design rests on. So we add fields to theirs.
    ⚠️ The def's class is the SUBCLASS `AlienWorlds.TidallyLocked.PlanetTypeDef`,
    so match on defName and never on the element name.

    HOW THE TWO FIELDS DIFFER (PlanetTypeManager.cs):
      :111-114  biomeBlacklist is the ALLOWED PREDICATE — a hard exclusion.
                Blacklist beats whitelist, and an EMPTY <biomes> means "all
                allowed", which is why <biomes> stays empty here.
      :123-124  biomeConfigs[x].scoreOffset is ADDED to BiomeWorker.GetScore —
                a soft competitive nudge, not an exclusion.

    ⚠️ <biomes> IS DELIBERATELY LEFT EMPTY, and this is the correction that
    matters most. A whitelist excludes everything absent from it — and the
    entries nobody thinks to list are the non-surface ones: Space, Orbit,
    Underground, Undercave, CQF_Undercave, AM_UndergroundSpace,
    VQEA_AncientComplex. Whitelisting would have silently broken space maps, the
    gravship's orbital layer and every pocket map. A blacklist fails toward "an
    unwanted biome appeared" — visible, one line to fix.

    🔴 THE OFFSET UNITS, MEASURED, BECAUSE THEY ARE NOT DIMENSIONLESS.
    BiomeWorker_Desert::Score is 13 bytes of IL and it is exactly:

        return tile.temperature + 0.0001f;

    THE SCORE IS DEGREES CELSIUS. On this planet's own curve that runs +70 at the
    subsolar point to -80 on the far nightside. So a scoreOffset of +10 buys ten
    degrees of competitive advantage, which is a large move, not a tweak.

    🔴 AND THE FLOOR IS THE TRAP. BiomeWorker_*::GetScore returns -100 for water
    and **0 when the biome is simply not Allowed**. So on the NIGHTSIDE, where
    temperatures are already negative, a big negative offset can push an ALLOWED
    biome below the 0 that a DISALLOWED one returns — and the disallowed biome
    wins the argmax. That inverts the intent silently.
    ⇒ Negative offsets are kept small. Do not deepen them past about -5 without
    re-deriving this; "rare" is expressed by the narrowness of each biome's own
    Allowed range far more than by our nudge.

      ABUNDANT  +12   a clear win wherever they are allowed at all
      COMMON     +4   tips close contests without dominating
      RARE       -4   loses head-to-head, still wins where it is the only
                      allowed biome — which is what "rare" should mean

    ⭐ AB_RockyCrags is COMMON on purpose, not abundant: the temperature curve
    already confines it to the dark hemisphere, so common yields a dark half
    rather than a planet-wide scatter.

    🔴 Ocean and Lake appear NOWHERE here, deliberately. They are
    isBackgroundBiome, assigned by the elevation threshold rather than by any
    worker score (BiomeWorker_Ocean::GetScore is `WaterCovered ? 0 : -100`), so a
    score offset cannot move them. Neither this patch nor anything we ship places
    them: the coastline is authored offline in ashkarr_paint.py and imported.

    ⏳ Not expressible as a flat offset: HorrorWastes and PoisonForest should form
    the dark MARGIN between twilight and full crags, and Glowforest should sit
    inside the deep night as isolated points of light. Frequency alone cannot say
    "at this latitude". ⛔ The workerClass override that would do it in-game is
    DEAD, not deferred (owner, 2026-08-19: nothing aimed at in-game worldgen
    survives). Place those biomes by hand in the painted map instead.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/AlienWorlds.TidallyLocked.PlanetTypeDef[defName="TidallyLocked"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/AlienWorlds.TidallyLocked.PlanetTypeDef[defName="TidallyLocked"]</xpath>
      <value>

        <biomeBlacklist>
          <li>ZBiome_CoastalDunes</li>
          <li>ZBiome_Sandbar_NoBeach</li>
          <li>ZBiome_Iceberg_NoBeach</li>
          <li>SeaIce</li>
          <li>ZBiome_Marsh</li>
          <li>TropicalRainforest</li>
          <li>ColdBog</li>
          <li>COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Cold</li>
          <li>COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Temperate</li>
          <li>TemperateSwamp</li>
          <li>TropicalSwamp</li>
          <li>Wetland</li>
          <li>Labyrinth</li>
          <li>MetalHell</li>
          <li>Savanna</li>
          <li>ZBiome_Grasslands</li>
          <li>Grasslands</li>
          <li>AB_GelatinousSuperorganism</li>
          <li>AB_IdyllicMeadows</li>
          <li>TemperateForest</li>
          <li>GlacialPlain</li>
          <li>AG_NereidPocketPlane</li>
          <li>AG_PocketPlane</li>
          <li>ZBiome_AlpineMeadow</li>
          <li>BorealForest</li>
          <li>ZBiome_CloudForest</li>
          <li>ZBiome_GlacialShield</li>
          <li>IceSheet</li>
          <li>Tundra</li>
        </biomeBlacklist>

        <biomeConfigs>
          <!-- ABUNDANT -->
          <ExtremeDesert><scoreOffset>12</scoreOffset></ExtremeDesert>
          <Desert><scoreOffset>12</scoreOffset></Desert>

          <!-- COMMON -->
          <ZBiome_Badlands><scoreOffset>4</scoreOffset></ZBiome_Badlands>
          <AridShrubland><scoreOffset>4</scoreOffset></AridShrubland>
          <Wasteland><scoreOffset>4</scoreOffset></Wasteland>
          <AB_RockyCrags><scoreOffset>4</scoreOffset></AB_RockyCrags>

          <!-- RARE -->
          <ZBiome_DesertOasis><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></ZBiome_DesertOasis>
          <AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle>
          <AB_MiasmicMangrove><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_MiasmicMangrove>
          <AB_MycoticJungle><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_MycoticJungle>
          <COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Tropical><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></COMIGO_GreaterSwamp_Tropical>
          <AB_OcularForest><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_OcularForest>
          <AB_TarPits><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_TarPits>
          <AB_PropaneLakes><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_PropaneLakes>
          <AB_MechanoidIntrusion><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_MechanoidIntrusion>
          <AB_GallatrossGraveyard><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_GallatrossGraveyard>
          <AB_PyroclasticConflagration><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></AB_PyroclasticConflagration>
          <Volcano><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></Volcano>
          <LavaField><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></LavaField>
          <Scarlands><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></Scarlands>
          <IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></IronScruff_PrimordialGeysers>
          <!-- RG_BoilingForest CUT 2026-08-15 — owner: "WE ARE NOT USING BOILING
               BIOME." regrowth.botr.boilingforest left the mod list in the
               585→575 descope, so this scored a def that no longer loads: it
               validated clean against the dump (which still carries 576 mods)
               and matched nothing in game. Do not re-add without the mod. -->
          <BMT_CrystalCaverns><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></BMT_CrystalCaverns>
          <BMT_EarthenDepths><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></BMT_EarthenDepths>
          <BMT_FungalForest><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></BMT_FungalForest>
          <HorrorWastes><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></HorrorWastes>
          <Glowforest><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></Glowforest>
          <PoisonForest><scoreOffset>-4</scoreOffset></PoisonForest>
        </biomeConfigs>

      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
